1|0@Design^1438964026#ctux0z7:TTUporter$:The fact you feel the need to hurl insults at other redditors on here, instead of actively trying to discuss opinions clearly points to your immaturity not just as a designer, but also as a person. I'm not even going to dignify those insults with a response. However, it needs to be said that there seems to be a disconnect between your ability to distinguish criticism from "talking shit", because the two are categorically different. Do I think this update is successful? Actually, yes I do. I think it is a nice update from the original shield that has aged pooly. However, I do think the execution, while successful, could still be more effective if the eye shape had been adjusted ever so slightly to make the animal appear less. Make the Nittany Lion have a furrowed brow, flatten the top of the eye shape to give off a feeling of stoicism. This looks like the Penn State that was caught off guard by the Sandusky scandal, not the Penn State that has strived to move on from that ordeal. Take it or leave it. No one here is making half of the claims you are claiming they are making. No one here is petitioning Penn State or Jerry Kuyper to go back and start from scratch. However, they are simply sharing their opinions on design on a design subreddit. Both professionals and amateurs, educated and laypersons. And from one professional designer to another, you should absolutely be ashamed of the way you are acting. Be a steward of our respective professions, or continue to watch both fade into ridicule and obsolescence. Educate, don't berate. 
1|0@Design^1438982516#ctv9f2k:lux_roth_chop$:Well, let's break down that insight you've delivered there, shall we? &gt; I do think the execution, while successful, could still be more effective if the eye shape had been adjusted ever so slightly to make the animal appear less. Make the Nittany Lion have a furrowed brow, flatten the top of the eye shape to give off a feeling of stoicism. Furrowed brow, scowling. Aggressive, hostile, angry. Well I did have a look at the institution in question but I didn't find anger, aggression or hostility in there anywhere. But that's by the by. What's really great about your comment - and I mean it, this is classic - is your cast iron conviction that the creative team who produced this logo *didn't think of changing the eye shape*. Because you are blessed with insight so superior and penetrating that you can see what they didn't. You know what? I bet they did try what you suggest and I bet it looked shit. Because the people who produced this are talented professionals who get hired to do top end branding projects, unlike you. &gt; Be a steward of our respective professions, or continue to watch both fade into ridicule and obsolescence. How will calling out the frauds and liars who can't even come up with a decent criticism hurt the industry? The design industry - well, your end of it anyway - is dying precisely because it's filled with fakes. It's dying because it needs to die; it's toxic and disgusting and deserves its reputation as a haven for crooks and scum. So let it go, and poke fun at the trash as they spiral into unemployment, confused at why they're losing yet another job when they have such n abundance of design skill that they can trash other people's work online.
